AI Invoice Auditor: 10-Commit Implementation Plan
Capstone window: 18 to 25 Sep 2026. This plan merges the problem statement (brief) and the Blueprint into one build order.

Every commit advances three parallel tracks. The tracks touch disjoint folders, so they can be built by three people, or interleaved by one, and merged without conflicts.

Track	Scope	Main folders
A: Ingestion & Persistence	monitor, extraction, translation, parsing, PostgreSQL, Redis, Qdrant writes, volumes	agent/agents/{monitor,extractor,translator,indexer}.py, agent/tools/, agent/db.py, db/
B: FastAPI & Streamlit	mock-erp service, agent HTTP API, dashboard, and the Dockerfiles for these services	mock-erp/, streamlit-ui/, agent/main.py
C: Agents & RAG	LangGraph graphs, validators, reporter, RAG agents, prompts, rules	agent/graph.py, agent/agents/{invoice_validator,business_validator,reporter}.py, agent/agents/rag/, agent/configs/
Every commit description below is self-contained: goal, what it relies on, per-track tasks, and an acceptance test.

1. Decisions and assumptions
The two source documents disagree in places, and neither is complete. This is how the plan resolves each point. Please confirm the ones marked ❓.

#	Topic	Decision	Why
D1	Compose filename	compose.yaml	The brief's deliverable list says compose.yaml. The Blueprint says docker-compose.yml. Compose v2 reads either.
D2	Config path	agent/configs/rules.yaml and persona.yaml, mounted read-only into the container	The brief says configs/. The Blueprint says config/. Mounting lets you tune tolerances without a rebuild.
D3	When to use Docker	Infra containers from Commit 1. Each app gets its Dockerfile in the commit where it first exists (mock-erp C2, streamlit and agent C3). Hardening in C9.	The Blueprint says "not Docker first", but brief §8.5 says build images one at a time. Finding network and permission bugs early is cheaper.
D4	Order of parse and translate	Extractor outputs raw text only. Translation runs next. Then parse_fields() runs on the English text.	This matches brief §5.1 (step 5 comes after step 4). The Blueprint puts parsed fields in the extractor's output.
D5	LLM use (brief §7.3 says validators use an LLM)	Verdicts stay deterministic (Decimal math). The LLM only does two narrow, cached assists: (a) repair a missing required field, accepted only if the value literally appears in the text; (b) vendor-name adjudication when fuzzy similarity is ambiguous. The Reporter uses the LLM for the narrative.	LLMs are unreliable at arithmetic. Every LLM call is optional and fails safe.
D6	Tolerance semantics	A mismatch is recorded only if its deviation is greater than the tolerance. Deviation is abs(invoice - erp) / erp * 100.	The brief says "flag beyond tolerance". The Blueprint example flags 4.17% against a 5% tolerance, which is inconsistent.
D7	Recommendation and re-validation	The brief marks both "need not be implemented". The recommendation is a small config-driven rule (about 15 lines). Re-validation is an optional Track C item in C8 and is the first thing cut.	The column exists in the suggested schema and the Blueprint's UI flow expects a button.
D8	Who writes human_feedback	The agent writes it through POST /feedback. The UI only reads PostgreSQL.	The brief's ownership table says the agent writes audit and the UI reads it.
D9	Report text for RAG	Add report_json JSONB and report_html TEXT to invoice_audit.	The brief says Qdrant must be rebuildable from PostgreSQL alone, so reports must live in PostgreSQL.
D10 ❓	Embedding model	Bedrock amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0 via LiteLLM (1024 dims, set in env).	The stack lists no embedding model. Local models (torch) would blow the 1.5 GB image budget. Confirm this is allowed, or switch to Cohere embed-multilingual.
D11	Language detection	One cheap Nova Lite call on the first 1,500 characters, cached in Redis.	No extra library, and it copes with noisy invoice text.
D12	Reranking	Deterministic heuristic (score plus source_type and invoice-number boosts, threshold, dedupe).	No extra model or library. Document the upgrade path (cross-encoder).
D13	Watching the folder	Poll with os.scandir every 3 s plus a "size and mtime unchanged" stability check.	It needs no watchdog library. inotify is unreliable on Docker Desktop bind mounts.
D14	Web framework style	Plain def endpoints and threads. No asyncio.	Simpler code and fewer libraries.
D15	incoming/ mount	Bind mount, read-only. Reports go to a named volume reports_data.	A non-root container cannot write to a host-owned bind mount. See the Check 4 caveat in C9.
D16	Retry count	"Max retries: 3" means up to 3 re-retrievals after the first attempt, so at most 4 generations.	Ambiguous in the brief. The value is configurable.
