3.3 mock-erp HTTP API (container port 8000)
Endpoint	200 body	404
GET /health	{"status":"ok"}, runs SELECT 1	n/a
GET /vendor/{vendor_id}	{vendor_id, name, currency, status}	{"detail":"vendor not found"}
GET /po/{po_number}	{po_number, vendor_id, currency, status, line_items:[{line_number, sku, description, quantity, unit_price}]}	same shape
GET /sku/{sku_code}	{sku, description, uom, list_price, currency, active}	same shape
The agent parses ERP JSON with resp.json(parse_float=Decimal). A 404 means "not in ERP" and becomes a discrepancy. Any 5xx or connection error raises ErpUnavailable, which fails the invoice with error. It never becomes a fake discrepancy.

