5. Working in parallel
Commit 1 freezes the contracts. After that, Track A, B and C never wait on each other within a commit, because each builds against the contract with stubs or fixtures.
Merge recipe: do each track on a short-lived branch (c04-track-a, and so on). Because folders are disjoint, merge them into one integration branch, run the acceptance test, then git merge --squash into main as one commit. Solo, work track by track and stage with git add -p.
Commit message format: type(scope): subject. Put the three track summaries in the body, and tag milestones v0.1 through v1.0.
Definition of done for every commit:
pytest is green.
docker compose up -d --build reaches all-healthy.
scripts/scan_secrets.sh (or the pre-commit hook) is clean.
README and CHANGELOG are updated.
