Track A: Ingestion & Persistence

agents/monitor.py, a polling watcher thread. Every MONITOR_POLL_SECONDS it scans the top level of INCOMING_DIR and applies these rules:
Ignore dotfiles and temp names (~$*, *.part, *.tmp, *.crdownload).
Stability check: a file counts as ready only when its size and mtime are unchanged across two consecutive polls. This protects against half-copied files.
Keep an in-memory (path, size, mtime) set so files are not re-hashed every poll.
A file is handed to the graph only when it is stable.
Monitor node in the graph:
Map the extension to the type: .pdf, .docx, .png. Anything else logs a file_events row with unsupported and stops.
Compute sha256 in 1 MB chunks.
Call db.claim_invoice(...). A None result means duplicate: log an audit.file_events row with duplicate (with the earlier path in detail), then end. Otherwise write a detected event.
If the file cannot be read or is 0 bytes, still record it: use sha256(path + "unreadable") as the synthetic checksum, set processing_status='error' with error_message, and log an error event.
Output state: {file_path, file_checksum, file_type, invoice_id, thread_id=invoice_id}.
db.py additions: log_file_event, set_status, mark_error. Node wrappers catch exceptions, call mark_error, and end the graph. A bad file must never kill the watcher.
