Track A: Ingestion & Persistence

tools/extraction_tools.py:
extract_pdf: use pdfplumber extract_text() per page. If the non-whitespace characters across all pages are below min_text_chars_per_page × pages, there is no usable text layer, so fall back to OCR with pdf2image.convert_from_path(dpi=300) and pytesseract.image_to_string(img, lang=OCR_LANGS) per page. Method is pdfplumber or tesseract.
extract_docx: use Document.iter_inner_content() (python-docx 1.x) to keep paragraphs and tables in document order. Join table cells with | and include section headers, because invoice numbers often sit there. Method is docx.
extract_image (PNG): open with Pillow, convert to grayscale, upscale if narrower than about 1,500 px, then run Tesseract with --psm 6. Method is tesseract.
On startup, assert OCR_LANGS ⊆ pytesseract.get_languages(). If not, fail fast.
agents/extractor.py is a node that dispatches by file_type. Store the text verbatim (only strip NUL bytes and normalise newlines). Persist raw_extracted_text and extraction_method through db.save_extraction, set status extracted, and use mark_error on failure.
