9. Viva cheat-sheet (the brief says to be prepared to explain these)
Scaling: mock-erp and streamlit-ui are stateless and scale horizontally. The agent can scale workers too, because ON CONFLICT (file_checksum) makes claiming a file atomic. PostgreSQL and Qdrant are stateful single nodes here and scale vertically, or with replication and clustering. Redis is a disposable cache.
LiteLLM in-process vs gateway: in-process is simpler and has no extra hop. In production a gateway centralises rate limits, cost tracking and credentials.
Restart policy: it recovers a crashed process but does not fix a bad start order, since it just loops. Ordering is fixed by health-gated depends_on.
Volumes vs object storage: a bind-mounted incoming/ is a development convenience. Production would use object storage with events, and the database would keep only the reference.
down vs down -v: -v deletes named volumes (pgdata, qdrant_data, reports_data). Without it, the data survives.
Why Redis holds nothing durable: if it is flushed the system only gets slower (translations and LLM answers are recomputed).
Why audit is separate from langgraph: checkpoints are working memory for resuming workflows, and they can be pruned. The audit trail is the business record.
Why SQL for structured questions: it is exact, cheap and needs no LLM. RAG is reserved for open-ended "why" questions.